A||N||6||fropuff||How long should I wait???||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||10-25-2000||05:16 PM||||Hey, I just got my GT painted in mid- to late August.  I was wondering how long I should wait until I wax it.  I've heard 90 days many times, but I'm still not sure.  Is this long enough?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-25-2000||05:20 PM||||I have heard that your suposed to wait at least 30 days.  Even after the paint is "dry" on a car, it actually is still curing.  If wax is put on too quickly, it will seal the wet paint in and not allow it to cure.  This would ruin the job. 30 may be the minumum, but 90 days should definately be long enough. <P>Hey, what color is it?  Do you have any pics?  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||10-25-2000||05:23 PM||||When I had my front repainted they said I had to wait 2 weeks before I could wash it... I don't think it would have mattered if I waited 3 months since they did a p!ss poor job anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||10-25-2000||05:51 PM||||I washed mine the day after I got it painted.  I was told that by the paint guy.  I also was told that I could start wet-sanding all the blemishes out 24 hours later.  Didn't seem to do anything.  I just didn't use a wash with wax in it.  Didn't hurt.  By the way, mine is red, of course!  You can see some pictures of it.  They're not good at all, crappy scanner.  There at:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003551.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003551.html</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 10-25-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-25-2000||08:15 PM||||best thing to do is check the recomendations for the specific paint from the manufacturer. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||10-25-2000||08:16 PM||||If they used Dupont paint, Dupont recomends that you wait at least 30days before waxing. I was in the body business for 5 years, I also went to school at Dupont in PA. I've heard that wax really isn't good for paint anyways, it seals the paint and doesn't allow it to breathe. I never really saw where it did any damage though, I've been waxing my cars ever since I can remember. I highly recomend Meguires products!!! Especially the expensive line, I believe it's their Gold series. <P><BR>Good Luck!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-25-2000||08:54 PM||||Ive had my own custom paint and body shop for 30 years now. I recommend on laquer and catylized paint to wait at least 30 days. Air dried acrylic enamel at least 90 days. I actually never wax my own cars, i just use occasional polish. I like Non Swirl Turtlewax Polish. I painted my car over 2 years ago and my Mercedes 9 years ago, they both still look like glass, and I drive them all the time, all weather. ||||reg||1
